import Googology.Trans.BMS.TrioFixU
import Googology.Trans.BMS.TrioRulesAllSheet

/-!
# Fix U against the sheet, with every check of `TrioRulesAllSheet`, and its own checks

`TrioFixU.lean` is `TrioRulesAll.lean` (rules 1–10 of
[koteitan/trio](https://github.com/koteitan/trio) with Fixes A–E and N) with rule 9
replaced by `MpsiLevelU` for an uncountable successor `u` of finite level.  This file
re-runs Parts 1–7 of `TrioRulesAllSheet.lean` for the patched rules
(`trioRuleMatrixOfAll`, `allOf`, `MAll`, `MstepAll`, `MfuelAll` replaced by
`trioRuleMatrixOfU`, `uOf`, `MU`, `MstepU`, `MfuelU`), then adds the patch's own guards
(Part 8).

* **The sheet**
  ([`tools/omega_alpha_rows.tsv`](https://github.com/koteitan/trio/blob/main/tools/omega_alpha_rows.tsv)):
  all guards of Parts 1–7 hold unchanged.  Fix U changes none of the 1,209 distinct
  labels used in them (Part 8), so every count is the one of `TrioRulesAllSheet.lean`.
  Part 7 (one step against rules 1–10) gets the same counts; on the `ψ` branch the step
  differs exactly when `fixAFires`, `fixEFires` or `fixUFires` holds, and `fixUFires`
  holds on none of the corpus labels.
* **Part 8.**  The 562 probe labels `ψ_{Ω_u}(Ω_w)` in the claimed domain (`inDomain`,
  14 values of `u`, from `Ω+1` to `Ω_4+1`): 0 order disagreements among them
  (157,641 pairs), and the 562 with the 784 chosen labels sorted by the order of the
  labels have their matrices in the same order.  Without Fix U (`TrioRulesAll`) the
  same 562 labels give 3,080 disagreements among themselves.  All 562 matrices are
  standard (yaBMS `bms -s`, outside Lean); without Fix U 337 are not.  The 1,303 probe
  labels outside the domain are listed too; nothing is claimed for them.
* **The new rows**, on one label each: the collapse row for `t = 2` (`ψ_1` and
  `ψ_{Ω_2}` arguments), for `Ω+1 < t ≤ u`, the table for `L = 2` (`P`, `P ++ mark`,
  `R_n` as expansions, the lifts, `Ω_Ω`), and for the lifts at `L = 2` the BM4
  expansion commutes with the construction on exactly the arguments where it does at
  `L = 1` (Fix E's case).

All of it is `#guard`s: a calibration, not a theorem.
-/

